# Under the app's minimum (640x480, X-MinSize): an older launcher ignores X-MinSize, so the shared runner shows the
# "needs 640x480" notice instead of the app, which closes on any key. 480x800 is a portrait panel the backend did not
# rotate (the harness has no rotation of its own: a rotated board gives the app its landscape size).
title Mesh Hop: screens under 640x480
env MESHHOP_DATA /tmp/mesh-hop-scene-data
env MESHHOP_PORT /nonexistent/ttyMH
env MESHHOP_ONLINE 0
sizes 480x320 800x400 640x400 480x800

shot notice
expect noquit
key down
expect quit
